    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0303" n="191" xml:id="pg191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/2004a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d186-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-21T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 21, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>883. Department’s July 11, 4 p.m., and instruction No. 6017 of July 15.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d186-f2"/> The American Government hopes that His Britannic
                    Majesty’s Government will be disposed to cooperate in the proposed international
                    consortium, more especially since the British Government has repeatedly urged
                    the formation of an American group to participate in loans to China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d186-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d186-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, on the same date, to the
                    Ambassador in France (No. 5382).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d186-f2" n="2" xml:id="d186-f2-content">
